WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
MAX SALTONSTALL: Welcome to
"BeyondCorp in a Bottle,"

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.666
where we explore
journeys into the world

00:00:03.666 --> 00:00:05.705
of context-aware access
and zero-trust networks.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.888
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:12.360
You've probably got
a list of employees

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.650
living in Active Directory
or some single sign-on

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.860
or LDAP equivalent.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:18.900
In order to enforce
your security policies

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:21.270
and take advantage of
context-aware access,

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.750
you'll need to create smarter
fine-grained controls.

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.340
Google's tools need to know
who's asking for access,

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.460
so we'll need to get
that identity information

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.590
into Google somehow.

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.190
The easy way, and what we do
at Google, is to use G Suite,

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.820
and then all your identities
already live in Google Cloud.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.590
If you want some extra
work, though, you

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:44.070
can always sync your identities
from your system to Google.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:45.930
Let's look at both options.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.910
For G Suite companies,
your identity already

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:50.100
lives on Google Cloud,
so Google Cloud Platform

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.010
can see all the users
and groups you've set up.

00:00:53.010 --> 00:00:54.490
Quick and easy.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:58.470
If you're on Active Directory
or OpenSSO, LDAP, et cetera,

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:00.720
then Google's Cloud
Directory Sync Tool

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.880
lets you quickly pull
your identity information

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.880
into Google Identity, enabling
you to make Cloud access

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.460
decisions based on group
memberships and user lists

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.330
that you already have.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:13.140
That's key to
context-aware access.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:18.090
Who you are matters and is more
important than where you are.

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:20.880
Without the who, we can't
make a good decision about

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.790
whether or not a given
request should be granted.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.800
Our migration to this
BeyondCorp inspired

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.640
model requires knowledge about
identity for each request.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.320
That's how Identity-Aware
Proxy can make

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.460
its person-based decisions.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.970
Let's say you decide your
first order of business

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.480
is to lock down your financial
tools to just folks in finance

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:42.330
to reduce the chance of
revenue data leaking.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.740
Your finance web
applications can

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.230
be protected by
Identity-Aware Proxy using

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.107
the identity groups you
brought into Google earlier.

00:01:49.107 --> 00:01:50.940
It's quick and easy to
restrict your payroll

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:53.160
app to only people
in the finance group

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:54.900
with just a few clicks.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:57.960
This system also lets you
automate updating access

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.950
when people change roles.

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:02.670
If I used to work in finance
then move over to legal,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.050
my payroll management
access should disappear.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:08.759
As soon as my groups are
updated within Google Identity,

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:11.039
IAP will enforce
the current policies

00:02:11.039 --> 00:02:13.590
based on my new memberships.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:16.530
Give it a try with one of the
various quick starts for IAP

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.650
or the guide for Cloud
Directory Sync linked below.

00:02:19.650 --> 00:02:21.840
To get more detail,
check out my blog post

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:23.970
for step-by-step
instructions and subscribe

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.910
to get more videos on
context-aware access.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.640
When it comes to protecting your
company, keep your data yours.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:32.990
[MUSIC PLAYING]

